    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d210-a7">

                <pb facs="1264" n="1106" sameAs="frus:frus1906p2/pg1106"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 5.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister for Foreign
                            Affairs to Ambassador Thompson</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of Foreign Affairs</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1907-01-09"><hi rendition="#italic">January 9,
                        1907</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ambassador</hi>: According to your excellency’s
                    desire I have the honor to inclose herewith the interrogatories<anchor n="a"
                        xml:id="d210-f1"/> prepared by the district judge of Yucatan, <pb
                        facs="1265" n="1107" xml:id="pg1107"/> in conformity with which should be
                    examined Alex Linoberry, Giovani Malfitano, and Chas. Spahlding, masters,
                    respectively, of the vessels <hi rendition="#italic">D. L. Trafton, Silas
                        Stearns</hi>, and <hi rendition="#italic">Lizzie B. Adams.</hi></p>
                <p>I avail, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Igno Mariscal.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
